# Today's scripts, scenes and data the rebuilt client runs, copied from godot/ at the same paths by tools/rebuild/sync-code.mjs (DECISIONS B43).
# One glob per line, relative to godot/; `!glob` leaves files out. `*` stays inside a folder, `**` crosses folders, a folder name takes it whole.
# Code files only (scripts and their uids, scenes, resources, shaders, data); assets go through client/assets.list. Never edit a copy in
# client/: change godot/ and sync, or port the file (--port). Left out on purpose: the per-creature systems the combat core replaces.

# ==== Copied: the game's code, scenes and data (whole folders; the leave-outs below take their parts out again)
audio      # AudioDirector (autoload), mixer, music, ambience, sample bank, the audio map
data       # content, combat, loot, progression and world JSON the rules and the core read
front      # login, character select, the front flow
fx         # Vfx (autoload), the Binbun controllers, primitives, the gallery
game       # avatar and creature rigs, boss telegraphs, event fx, inventory, loadout, settings, gathering and labor views
game_ui    # the panel host, tooltips, chat commands, tips, mock game
loot_view  # the loot drop view
main       # boot, audio hooks, camera rig, crash watch, assets pack loader, perf overlay
net        # API client, config, kill reporter, update check, mock backend
next       # the game scene folder: its non-seam parts (HUD parts, area milestones, depths, hub NPCs, rewards, world)
rules      # combat, loot, gear, progression, gathering and inventory rules
session    # DmSession and its bodies
sim        # pure sim helpers: nav, depths floors and rules, boss brains, exact math, shared constants
ui         # theme, HUD kit, panels, widgets, onboarding
world      # world builder, model loader, occlusion shaders, animator
world_fx   # world dressing and atmosphere

# ==== Ported (client/code.lock.json "ported"; edited in client/, so the sync leaves them alone and reports one whose original changed)
# next/next_game.gd, next/next_game.tscn   the game scene on DmCoreHost: a solo run in the Graves with a test-server character or a dev one, with the Gravecaller's rites and the seven bosses (the Covenant Seal's BossMeta in the value step); refuses any api but the test server's; the warm-up on request (opts.warmup); host or guest of a 2-player party (a puppet core on the guest), the friends list, online for friends' presence; value on the server on the host (rewards, meta, Chronicle, progression, the loot node); today's HUD and panels (DmGameUi); an enemy's chill, root and drag reach the hero (`_on_target_effect`); the four necromancers and the Reaper; the Chapterhouse; gathering (the Gather node on every peer before a guest's relay hold is released, the Acre's glue on the host with the HUD, the Acre ledger's panels warmed); the Depths (DmDepths, host only); the counsel's `world_entered` and a joiner's notice at the end of start; the crowd's cost options (lod_distances, reserve, cull, anim_lod, thrall_shadows) pass to the core host
# next/next_world.gd                       loads client/areas/<id>.tscn (every area but the Depths) and its navigation map instead of the runtime DmWorldBuilder build; the same small API, today's seals and gates (set_unlocked, set_door_open); gives the core its copy of the navmesh (bind_core); the Depths as an instance with no scene (open_instance, area_at, attach_floor / detach_floor: the floor's navmesh region goes to the core); hands the lights-only builder the two members the gathering views read: `area_nodes` (each area's root) and `node_views` (each GatherNodes holder); `door_opened` (a door rose: the gate sound), which `set_unlocked(areas, quiet)` keeps silent for the state a joining guest is given
# next/chapterhouse/dm_chapterhouse.gd     the gates and navmesh regions are DmNextWorld's (same names as the builder's); the people only with the Chapterhouse loaded; a waystone recalls the thralls through the core's legion; the party's guest has the host's seals (`apply_seals` and `check_seals` do nothing on a guest; `announce_seal` is the banner the host and a guest both show)
# next/next_input.gd                       the cursor's ground point every frame (today's took it with the 10 Hz hover pick, and the reticle stepped); the hover pick asks the core; the chase and the queued casts are today's (DmCombatInput); Easy auto combat is back (`auto`, closed until the settings or a gate_probe open it)
# next/spawn/dm_wave_director.gd           spawns through the core (ids); counts from the core; `off` leaves defs out (the parity scenario drops the Bellringers' censer, as today's side does); no Grave Surges; a ground left behind sends its living bodies away through the core (`remove_enemy`), as today's freed them; `over.aggro / leash` reach the body in the core (the Depths' hunters)
# next/hero/dm_hero_body.gd                an external of the core; enemy blows arrive by id (EV_TARGET_HIT), a chill, root or drag by `dm_enemy_effect` (EV_TARGET_EFFECT); no collider; thralls counted by the core
# next/hero/dm_hero_look.gd                the hovered-enemy ring reads the core by id and follows the drawn body (the crowd's interpolated place, every frame)
# next/enemy_fx/dm_enemy_fx.gd             an event consumer: the core's telegraphs, strikes, deaths, zones (dust and burning ground) and affix moments, the Pyre's and the Fen's sparks, embers and idle motes (no node per enemy); the thralls' sounds (thrallRise on thrall_raised, thrallDeath on thrall_died "killed": DmThrall's); a body removed alive swings no more
# game/dm_avatar.gd                        its own three motion helpers instead of DmEntityViews'
# game/dm_event_fx.gd, game/dm_event_fx_zones.gd   zone and corpse records read by field name (no DmSimZone, DmSimCorpse)
# main/main.gd, main/main.tscn             the boot (DmMain): the front flow against the TEST server, then the game scene with the chosen character, its bag and progression (DmMain.load_build); `--benchmark` and the Benchmark button (the run is sent to the test server only); the party hand-over (join_ready, client_ended, a failed join); the panels' Log out, Switch character and discipline change; no crash report
# net/dm_config.gd                         the TEST server's, lobby's and relay's addresses and the allow-list (DmConfig.allows_url, allows_api_base, allows_lobby_url, allows_relay); the live ones never appear (tests/front.gd)
# net/dm_http_transport.gd                 refuses any request DmConfig does not allow
# Easy auto combat and the benchmark (client/README.md "The benchmark"):
# next/feel/dm_next_auto.gd                the adapter reads the core: the bulk arrays (enemy_ids / positions / states, corpse_ids / positions) and the facts the host's signals keep (radius, elite, health, wind-up, corpse kind, hostile zones); same decisions, same intents
# game/dm_auto_combat.gd                   the same decisions (the golden cases of godot/tests/game pass, and 4,300 mutated real contexts agree with the original) at a quarter of the cost: native sorts, each field read once, the counting rites on packed arrays (a choice 3.0 ms on the VPS, 0.8; a step of the walk 0.8, 0.3)
# next/perf/dm_benchmark.gd                today's nine rooms and five classes (a room or class outside them is refused); the core's step, crowd sync and event dispatch per tick timed (DmCoreHost.measure) for the report's budget section; the HUD's share; the run's files in `DmBenchmark.dir`; the crowd's cost settings and per-frame counters in the report (`Crowd:` and `Crowd per frame`), `--bench-crowd=` to change them for a run; the frame's physics and process parts averaged (DmFrameSplit) beside Godot's peak monitors
# main/perf_overlay.gd                     the logic line is the frame's average process and physics part (DmFrameSplit, client-only: next/perf/dm_frame_split.gd), not Godot's peak monitors
# next/perf/dm_bench_fight.gd              boots the game scene with the room's area alone; the counts are held through the core (top_up through the director, trim by remove_enemy, thralls raised into the core)
# next/perf/dm_benchmark_screen.gd, next/perf/dm_benchmark_setup.gd   the budget section on the results; the upload note names the test server; the last setup in `DmBenchmark.dir`; a headless run quits by itself
# next/perf/dm_next_warmup.gd, game/dm_warmup.gd   the boss models, effects and gear drawn once, every crowd model from rehearsal rows, the area tour; no per-creature bodies (DmWarmup's old own warm-up is gone); on request only
# Graphics presets (client/README.md "Graphics presets", DECISIONS B45):
# game/dm_graphics_preset.gd               today's four presets on Forward+: no prop-light count or prop shadow range (baked), ambient occlusion, the crowd's shadow policy, apply_environment
# next/perf/dm_next_perf.gd                applies a preset to the game scene: moon, environment, viewport, the crowd's shadow policy (through CrowdView, so a benchmark run can override whether thralls cast) and the moon's direction for the crowd's culling, fx; Auto resolution upscales with FSR 1; no caster poll
# next/perf/dm_bench_history.gd            the history and the queue of runs to send live in `DmBenchmark.dir` (a test keeps its own); a script run never sends through a real transport (`flush`); the frame split rows (process_avg_ms, physics_avg_ms, physics_worst_ms) are lower-is-better
# 2-player co-op (client/README.md "Co-op on the core"):
# next/next_net.gd                         the core's snapshot (cut by body ranges to fit a packet), reliable batches and baseline over the session's peer, the heroes' ids and vitals, a guest's request for a baseline; no enemy dictionaries or cues (the core's events carry them)
# next/party/dm_next_party.gd              the lobby link, hosting, joining, invites and asks against the TEST lobby and relay (DmConfig), friendship changes announced (friends_changed), the host's world (heat, difficulty) told to the lobby, the host <-> guest handshake of the guest's own account (B22), party chat and announcements, ground drops between members (sends go to connected guests one by one), the host's seals told to a joining guest and to every guest when they change (`send_seals`)
# session/dm_session.gd                    the hello carries the core's wire version (DmCore.wire_version(), PROTOCOL 3) and the host refuses another; `abort(reason)` for a guest the host's messages cannot be used by
# The bosses (client/README.md "The bosses"): a boss is an external of the core (kind 1) whose brain stays GDScript; the brains of sim/bosses are copies, unchanged:
# next/bosses/dm_boss.gd                   a plain node (no DmEnemy, no collider, no agent, no state machine) that registers as an external of the core (core_id) and takes blows through take_damage
# next/bosses/dm_boss_host.gd              summon rules and events as today, all seven areas served; the thralls' blows come from the core (thrall_hit_external); no pool nodes (a boss's pools are core zones)
# next/bosses/dm_boss_node_world.gd        the brain's world on the core: adds through the director's spawn (a kind the core does not run yet is skipped), remove_enemy, set_enemy_hp, the core's thralls and corpses, pools as core zones, no vows (echoes() is the world's)
# next/bosses/dm_boss_fx.gd                no pool_visual (a boss's pools are drawn by DmEnemyFx from the core's zone events)
# game/dm_boss_view.gd                     its own three motion helpers instead of DmEntityViews'
# Copied again because of them: next/bosses/dm_boss_meta.gd (the Covenant Seal altar choice: made by the game scene's value step, with the boss key prompt of the HUD).
# Copied again because of them: next/status (DmStatusSet, for the status sets of heroes and bosses only), next/enemy_fx/dm_enemy_fx_host.gd, game/dm_event_fx_telegraph.gd,
# game/dm_event_fx_boss.gd, next/progress/dm_next_chronicle.gd, next/areas/dm_area_flow.gd (the area and procession banners: the game scene makes it).
# Gathering and the Acre (client/README.md "Gathering and the Acre"): the Gather node (next/gathering/dm_next_gather.gd), the loop, the node views, the skills and the laborers' views (game/dm_gather_loop.gd,
# dm_node_views.gd, dm_skills.gd, dm_laborer_views.gd) are copies, unchanged: a node is an area scene's prop and a laborer one of at most four pooled models in the Acre, never a body of the core. The Acre's glue is a port:
# next/gathering/dm_next_acre.gd           the laborer views read the lights-only builder of DmNextWorld (`game.world.builder`: its `world` is the world.json data) where today's reads the game's builder, which does not exist here (the area is a scene)
# The HUD and the panels on the core (client/README.md "The HUD on the core"; its draw-call budget: "The HUD's budget"; DECISIONS B46: DmGameUi and the panels are copies):
# next/hud/dm_next_ui_host.gd              the host-contract adapter: the core host's events instead of each enemy's (numbers, elites, the counsel's facts), the target by id, the bag and the drops the loot node's, no Altar (B36)
# next/hud/dm_next_counsel.gd              the counsel's host side (the busy flags and the 400 ms poll's facts) asks the core on the poll: three living dead within 9 m, the corpses within 7 m, a pack of three on a corpse, the thralls he owns; no DmEnemy, DmCorpseField or DmThrallHost; the bosses' summon sites per area and the doors' rects are read once, not on every poll
# ui/onboarding/dm_counsel_events.gd      `tick_calls` takes `altar` (default true, today's); the rebuilt poll says false (no Altar of Ascension, DECISIONS B36), which holds back the vows, altar_unlocks and boons tips
# main/audio_hooks.gd                      the gate sound is the world's `door_opened` signal, not a poll of every door each frame; the rest (listener, area bed and music, footsteps, the boss switch) is today's
# next/hud/dm_next_hud_vm.gd               the view-model from the core's bulk arrays (target frame, minimap dots, thrall count, corpses near the hero, cooldowns); no DmThrallHost, DmEnemy or DmCorpseField; its host is the adapter; the Depths readout, the minimap's floor and the area line, and the hub's prompt; the hero's caster, soul state and rite level looked up once per refresh, not per slot
# game/dm_game_hud.gd                      only the art path and the interaction prompts: the old game's view-model builder (DmSimEnemy) is gone
# ui/hud/dm_hud.gd                         the pieces (movable, scalable: set_piece, set_layout, show_piece), drawn from one atlas on z layers, floats from a pool; the left readouts (ward, Kill Chain, belt, omen, party) are applied by section of their own, so a moving chain meter applies nothing else
# ui/hud/dm_hud_kit.gd                     the layers (Z_PANEL .. Z_FLOATS), plate / rect / outline / gradient_rect from the atlas, the draw-call model's log; `style` still gives a StyleBoxFlat (copied panels ask for it); the text of `commas` is kept per number
# ui/hud/dm_hud_bar.gd, dm_hud_parts.gd, dm_hud_orb.gd, dm_hud_slot.gd, dm_hud_minimap.gd, dm_hud_brew_chip.gd   rectangles from the atlas, vector art as one mesh per widget, the dots as a MultiMesh;
#                                          the animated edges are layers drawn once and faded by their alpha (the NEW glow's halo in dm_hud_parts.gd, a slot's empowered pulse and cast flash in dm_hud_slot.gd: a frame costs a property, not
#                                          a redraw), a slot whose rite only moved along its cooldown changes its seconds and sweep and nothing else, the low-health wash processes only while it moves
# ui/widgets/dm_toast.gd, dm_banner.gd, dm_corners.gd   a 9-patch panel and atlas rectangles
# Client-only files beside them (not copies): next/hud/dm_hud_atlas.gd (the runtime atlas), dm_hud_mesh.gd (triangle bags), dm_hud_floats.gd (the pool of floating numbers).
# The panel host's per-frame questions (client/README.md "The HUD's budget", CPU): what the HUD and the counsel ask every few frames is answered without a scan:
# game_ui/dm_game_ui.gd                    panel_open() from a flag the windows' own visibility changes set (also asked by the combat input a dozen times a second), area_safe() per area, the Ascension guidance asks the
#                                          Prelate count before it builds a progression and keeps the Swift Seals share and the parsed trophies until their sources change
# next/progress/dm_next_belt.gd            the belt chips' bag counts, picks and Dry Cellar answer are made again only when the bag was replaced, a pick changed or the vows did (one pass over the bag, not thirty)
# ui/onboarding/dm_counsel.gd              the clock waits for the earliest timer due instead of scanning the timers every frame; a card on screen is only compared with the urgent and danger tips waiting (the only ones that can take its place), not the whole line
# ui/widgets/dm_tip_card.gd                the draining line is drawn once and squeezed by a scale (`show_timer`) instead of 24 rectangles every frame
# ui/onboarding/dm_counsel_view.gd         the card's line is `show_timer`; its fade and mouse filter are set when they change, not every frame
# game_ui/dm_game_ui.gd (also)             the counsel asks the host for the legion's size (`thralls_now`) when it checks the first-thrall card, not for a whole view-model
# The Gravecaller's rites on the core (client/README.md "The Gravecaller's rites"): enemies are ids and DmFoe snapshots, a blow is `c.deal`, a status `c.apply_status`, the corpse field
# is core/dm_core_corpses.gd and the legion core/dm_core_legion.gd (the core's own, not copies):
# next/rites/dm_rite_caster.gd, dm_rite_module.gd, dm_rite_legends.gd   the plumbing (the registry, dm_rite_registry.gd, is a copy again since the Reaper came)
# next/rites/rite_*.gd  (24 of the 25; rite_veil_step.gd needed no change and is a copy)   black_litany, bone_fan, bone_mantle, bone_needle, bone_prison, bone_storm, carrion_seed, command_rend,
#                                          corpse_explosion, dirge, exhume, grave_frost, grave_hands, grave_offering, grave_step, ivory_cleave, marrow_spear, miasma, ossuary_wall (the wall is not solid
#                                          for the core's enemies yet), plague_bloom, rally_dead, rot_lance, soul_siphon, wailing_skull
# next/feel/dm_combat_input.gd             the attack target is the core's enemy id; the caster says whether it is alive and hittable
# Copied again because of them: next/rites/dm_rite_hotbar.gd, next/rites/rite_veil_step.gd, next/progress/dm_next_belt.gd.
# The Reaper (client/README.md "The Gravecaller's rites"): her shared helper and three rites ported as the necromancer's (DmFoe snapshots, `c.deal`, `c.apply_status`):
# next/rites/dm_reaper_rites.gd, rite_scythe_weave.gd, rite_wraith_walk.gd, rite_unleash_souls.gd; her other five rites are copies, and game/dm_rite_fx.gd is a copy again.
# Value on the server (client/README.md "Value on the server"): kills are the game's `kill_credited`, the bag is the game's `loot` (client-only next/rewards/dm_next_loot.gd:
# today's DmNextUiHost take, pickup, claim and rune-ownership paths on their own):
# next/rewards/dm_session_rewards.gd       kills from `kill_credited` (the killer is a peer), lifesteal from DmCoreHost.struck; no watch_enemy / attach_spawner
# next/meta/dm_next_meta.gd                a kill's enemy is a core id; no vows, heat or Covenant Boons (DECISIONS B36: no Bonded Dead); the Reaper's soul wisp bursts through a local, not the node (a wisp can arrive after the game is gone)
# next/progress/dm_next_progress.gd        the bag is the loot node's (the server's rows until it exists)
# next/areas/dm_wave_milestones.gd         the Nightfall light dims the world's lights (DmNextWorld.builder); banners through the game's `game_event`
# next/party/dm_next_joiner.gd             a party guest's own account; its bag is the loot node's
# next/progress/dm_next_codex.gd          a spawn is the core host's enemy_spawned (an id, its def and place)
# The Depths (client/README.md "The Depths"): the instanced descent below the world, its floors generated, drawn and baked at run time:
# next/depths/dm_depths.gd                 the controller on the core: its dead are core ids (the core's spawned, died and removed events keep the Depths' living set; remove_enemy takes every body of the Depths out), corpses through the core's field, the hero's thralls recalled through the caster; the floor is baked first and swapped in one frame; the HUD's readout and map are kept in place; no warm-up (the crowd's baked models are the core's)
# next/depths/dm_depths_ground.gd          the floor's navmesh baked on a worker thread (NavigationServer3D, the builder's settings) and handed to the core (DmNextWorld.attach_floor); the picture is the lights builder's build_depths_floor; no physics colliders
# next/depths/dm_depths_run.gd             the floor can be handed in already generated (the controller makes it on a worker thread)
# The effects (client/README.md "The benchmark"; native/README.md "Files"):
# fx/dm_fx_ring.gd                         the motes and the per-frame loop are the core's DmMotes (C++); the random start of each mote is still made here (client/tests/fx_motes.gd)

# ==== Per-creature systems the combat core and the crowd view replace: not copied (DECISIONS B42, B43)
!enemies                      # DmEnemy, its states, kinds and scenes: the core owns enemies
!sim/sim_enemy.gd             # DmSimEnemy record
!sim/sim_thrall.gd            # DmSimThrall record
!sim/sim_corpse.gd            # DmSimCorpse record
!sim/sim_zone.gd              # DmSimZone record
!next/thralls                 # DmThrall, DmThrallHost and the thrall scenes
!next/corpses                 # DmCorpseField
!next/affixes                 # DmAffixSet
!game/dm_entity_views.gd      # DmEntityViews: per-creature nodes, replaced by the crowd view

# ==== Seams: ported to the core in later steps (each uses a per-creature class or scene)
!game/dm_caster_budget.gd                 # uses DmEnemy, DmEnemyState
!main/qa_driver.gd                        # uses DmEnemy
!next/areas/dm_grave_surge.gd             # uses DmEnemy

# ==== Left out with a seam (main/qa_driver.gd)
!main/qa_boot.gd                          # uses qa_driver

# ==== Left out: the boss is a plain node in the port (next/bosses/dm_boss.gd), made by DmBossHost; this scene was a CharacterBody3D with a collider and a navigation agent
!next/bosses/boss.tscn

# ==== Left out: today's minimal HUD host (the rebuilt client's HUD is today's DmGameUi on DmNextUiHost, DECISIONS B46)
!next/next_hud.gd

# ==== Left out: the screenshot and QA tools of today's game (main/qa_driver.gd's chain)
!game_ui/shoot.gd                         # the screenshot tool
!game_ui/shoot.tscn                       # uses shoot
!main/qa_ui_shots.gd                      # uses the QA driver

